<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Strike at Chromecorp mine ends.</title>
<headline>Strike at Chromecorp mine ends.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Union of Mineworkers (NUM) said on Wednesday 1,000 workers at the Chromebronne Mining Division and Cashane Plant had ended a eight-day strike.</p>
<p>The mine is owned by Chromecorp Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>The strike, which began on January 20, followed a failure to reach agreement with management on wages and working conditions.</p>
<p>But the NUM said in a statement on Wednesday that the mine management and union representatives had reached agreement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The company agreed to meet the union demands of 11 to 15 percent increase,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The NUM wanted a 12-15 percent rise, while management has offered nine to 10 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
